ormulation of the Objective**:\n   We now need to prove:\n   \\[\n   a_{1} x_{1} + b_{1} y_{1} + c_{1} z_{1} \\geqslant 0\n   \\]\n   From equations (1) and (2), it suffices to show:\n   \\[\n   (a_{1} + x_{1})^2 + (b_{1} + y_{1})^2 + (c_{1} + z_{1})^2 \\geq 4\n   \\]\n\n6. **Applying the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality**:\n   Using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we get:\n   \\[\n   (a_{1} + x_{1})^2 + (b_{1} + y_{1})^2 + (c_{1} + z_{1})^2 \\geq \\frac{1}{3} \\left(a_{1} + b_{1} + c_{1} + x_{1} + y_{1} + z_{1}\\right)^2\n   \\]\n   Moreover, applying the AM-GM inequality to \\(a_{1} + b_{1} + c_{1}\\) and \\(x_{1} + y_{1} + z_{1}\\), we get:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{3} \\left[ (a_{1} + b_{1} + c_{1}) + (x_{1} + y_{1} + z_{1}) \\right]^2 \\geq \\frac{4}{3} (a_{1} + b_{1} + c_{1})(x_{1} + y_{1} + z_{1}) = \\frac{4}{3} \\cdot 3 = 4\n   \\]\n\n7. **Conclusion**:\n   From steps (6) and (7), we conclude that:\n   \\[\n   (a_{1} + x_{1})^2 + (b_{1} + y_{1})^2 + (c_{1} + z_{1})^2 \\geq 4\n   \\]\n   which implies:\n   \\[\n   a_{1} x_{1} + b_{1} y_{1} + c_{1} z_{1} = a x + b y + c z \\geq 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{a x + b y + c z \\geq 0}\n   \\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Consider an alphabet of 2 letters. A word is any finite combination of letters. We will call a word unpronounceable if it contains more than two of the same letter in a row. How many unpronounceable 7-letter words are there?", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, so I need to figure out how many 7-letter words are unpronounceable given that the alphabet has 2 letters. Unpronounceable here is defined as having more than two of the same letter in a row. That means any word with three or more identical consecutive letters is considered unpronounceable. So the task is to count all such 7-letter words over a 2-letter alphabet that have at least one instance of three identical letters in a row.\n\nFirst, let me make sure I understand the problem corre